[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "King's Gambit Declined"]
[Variation "King's Gambit Declined: Classical Variation"]
[ECO "C30"]
[Character "tactical"]
[Risk "high"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "trap,fork"]
[Themes "queen-check,fork-king-rook"]
[Refutes "1. e4 e5 2. f4 Bc5 3. fxe5 Qh4+"]
[Kind "against-us"]

1. e4 e5 2. f4 Bc5 3. fxe5? { Takes a pawn but leaves the f-file and the king exposed, because nothing guards h4 and g3. } 3... Qh4+ { Check from the queen. The king cannot go forward and has to deal with it. }
4. g3? { Blocks the check, but the pawn on e4 is now unprotected and the rook on h1 sits on the same diagonal behind it. } 4... Qxe4+ { The queen takes the e4 pawn with check and attacks the rook on h1 at the same time: a fork of king and rook. }
5. Qe2 Qxh1 *
